# JavaScript Random Quote Generator

Project 8 of my 30 JavaScript Projects Challenge.

A responsive Quote Generator built using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript that fetches random quotes from an API and provides features for copying quotes, switching themes, and handling loading states.

---

## Features

- Generate random quotes from an API
- Display quotes with their authors
- Dark and light mode toggle
- Theme persistence using Local Storage
- One-click copy to clipboard
- Loading state while fetching data
- Fallback quote when API requests fail
- Fully responsive design
- Smooth UI interactions

---

## Architecture Approach

The application uses asynchronous API requests and dynamic DOM manipulation to fetch, display, and manage quotes.

- JavaScript fetches random quotes using the Fetch API
- `async/await` handles asynchronous operations
- Loading states provide feedback while quotes are being fetched
- Error handling displays a fallback quote if an API request fails
- The Clipboard API allows users to copy quotes
- Theme preferences are stored in Local Storage and persist after reloading

---

## Tech Stack

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Fetch API
- Clipboard API
- Local Storage API
- Quote API

---

## What I Learned

- Using the Fetch API with `async/await`
- Handling API errors gracefully
- DOM manipulation and event handling
- Implementing clipboard functionality
- Managing theme preferences with Local Storage
- Writing clean and reusable JavaScript logic
- Working with external APIs

